    "translations": {
      "en": {
        "title": "Return and replacement logistics",
        "summary": "Review original outbound, exchange and reshipment cases with their shipment and tracking fields.",
        "category": "After-sales",
        "keywords": [
          "Return and replacement logistics",
          "after-sales",
          "native integration"
        ],
        "sections": {
          "steps": [
            "Review original outbound, exchange and reshipment cases with their shipment and tracking fields.",
            "Verify items, quantities, physical handoff and destination before the original logistics action. Creation, carrier handoff and delivery require separate evidence."
          ],
          "boundaries": [
            "The source module must be enabled and bound to the selected company, using an existing active source account. Company-wide ERP access and dedicated module grants intersect with the source role; no account or authority is created automatically.",
            "A non-administrator ERP actor uses the source admin role only with all 19 explicit after-sales integration grants (nine read/update pairs plus audit read), ENTITY company scope and an existing active source admin account. This grants no native ERP ADMIN/SUPER_ADMIN, wildcard or cross-company authority. Modules and each write still intersect explicit grants with current source permissions. Missing any grant retains the operational role; an existing source admin account cannot widen it.",
            "The same after-sales case retains the original forms, controls, attachments, errors and workflow. Opening a page or authenticating does not prove a business operation is complete. Save unsaved forms or explicitly discard them before leaving.",
            "Read access does not grant writes. Submissions recheck source role, dedicated ERP write permission and current state. This guide adds no AI execution tool and proves no external message, payment, refund, logistics or stock operation.",
            "Each launch uses its own iframe; responses from an earlier company or entry are ignored. Initial readiness checks the current frame, same-origin mount and requested path. A load error or missing readiness after 45 seconds exposes an error and retry; neither an old page nor an error response proves successful integration.",
            "Logout on a fixed same-origin ERP DEV entry first clears the after-sales HttpOnly session cookie and numeric chunks, then completes existing WMS and ERP logout. A three-second timeout or clear failure retains ERP login for retry. A new login also clears the old session before authenticating or writing a new JWT; failed startup authentication tries clearing before removing the invalid local JWT. Clearing works while the source is unavailable or the module is disabled. Actual browser login, logout and reopening still require acceptance.",
            "Original React Server Action forms remain business drafts even when their DOM method reports GET; explicit POST and source action markers are also protected. Ordinary GET search/filter forms are not business drafts. Submission, failure or preview alone does not clear unsaved state; preserve the form until explicit discard. Actual browser back, cancellation and failed submission require candidate acceptance.",
            "Confirmation dialogs and save feedback use the current page React context. Cancelling departure preserves the form; switch only after explicit discard. Save feedback does not replace a successful backend result or prove notification, payment or physical acceptance.",
            "Original repair entry accepts only /cases?type=REPAIR&queue=technician. Reshipments, exchange returns, refund pickups and private purchases each accept only their corresponding /cases?type=RESHIPMENT, EXCHANGE_RETURN, REFUND_PICKUP or PRIVATE_PURCHASE redirect. Initial readiness requires the current requested section, exact parameter count and values, current frame, company, same-origin mount and reported path; duplicate, extra, hash or cross-section aliases are rejected. Role and write checks remain required."
          ],
          "related": [
            "after-sales-native-cases",
            "personal-inbox"
          ]
        }
      }
    },
